OpenBSD uses the generic ps-based process identity. Keep its lstart string
independent of the invoking client's locale and timezone so start/stop from
different terminals can verify the same daemon. Other platforms are unchanged.

Index: codex-rs/app-server-daemon/src/backend/pid.rs
--- codex-rs/app-server-daemon/src/backend/pid.rs.orig
+++ codex-rs/app-server-daemon/src/backend/pid.rs
@@ -732,8 +732,11 @@
 
